WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:04.413
- [Mark] So Norman.

00:00:04.413 --> 00:00:05.246
- Yes.

00:00:05.246 --> 00:00:06.580
- [Mike] It's been a week or so.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:08.413
How many days has it been since we talked?

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:12.738
- [Norman] I think it was
last Tuesday when we talked

00:00:12.738 --> 00:00:13.970
- [Mark] So it's been a week and a half

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:16.152
- [Norman] Yeah about a week and a half.

00:00:16.152 --> 00:00:17.370
- [Mark] And what's going on?

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:19.760
- [Norman] Well, what's transpired is

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:24.350
I looked at all the comments
and they were heartfelt.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:27.260
They were very inspiring to the point

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.470
to where you're looking at a man

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:32.050
who has compiled eight
days sober as of today.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.080
- [Mark] You haven't used in eight days?

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:34.280
- Eight days.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:37.640
No beer, no marijuana,
no crack, no nothing.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:38.910
- [Mark] Wow. That's impressive.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:40.050
- I don't know if you guys can tell,

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:42.594
but my face is fatter because
I've just been eating.

00:00:42.594 --> 00:00:43.910
(chuckles)

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.500
I've been eating a lot.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:46.333
- [Mark] That's what happens.

00:00:46.333 --> 00:00:48.010
- But I feel really good, you know?

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:48.843
- [Mark] Yeah. You sound different.

00:00:48.843 --> 00:00:49.676
You called me last night.

00:00:49.676 --> 00:00:53.708
You just sound like so clear,
like you could just tell.

00:00:53.708 --> 00:00:54.541
- Yeah it's there.

00:00:54.541 --> 00:00:57.610
I mean, and it was attributed

00:00:57.610 --> 00:00:59.970
to the comments that I got, and...

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:01.850
- [Mark] Yeah, you got
a lot of positivity.

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:04.290
- And also that good word.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.586
It was the wherewithal within myself.

00:01:06.586 --> 00:01:07.419
- [Mark] That's my favorite word.

00:01:07.419 --> 00:01:08.700
- And I said, you know what?

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.360
I really don't want to do this anymore.

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:13.410
I mean, I have people
who don't even know me

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:17.400
that listened to me and they gave me hope.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.300
They gave me inspiration.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.930
And I truly believe that
when your hope is reborn,

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:23.743
so is an opportunity
to transform your life.

00:01:23.743 --> 00:01:25.610
So my hope is being reborn

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:27.770
and my self-esteem is being rebuilt

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:29.223
because you have to look at self esteem.

00:01:29.223 --> 00:01:31.690
It's self esteem.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:34.850
So therefore, no one else
can knock me down but me.

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:36.440
So what do I want to do?

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:37.940
And here I am.

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:38.773
- [Mark] That's great.

00:01:38.773 --> 00:01:41.720
I think you were ready perhaps,

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:43.075
and this was maybe just the impetus

00:01:43.075 --> 00:01:44.490
to get your shit together.

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:45.640
- Yeah, I think it was one of those things

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:48.980
where I had to really
talk about the issues.

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:50.450
One person had mentioned in a comment

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:51.720
maybe I need to see a therapist.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.451
And I'm looking into that.

00:01:53.451 --> 00:01:54.470
- [Mark] I think that's always great.

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:58.723
- I really want to, I really
want to do something better.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:01.990
Also I have some other good news.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:04.140
Tuesday, I have a video interview.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:04.973
- [Mark] For a job.

00:02:04.973 --> 00:02:09.392
- For a job as a property
manager of 11 different units.

00:02:09.392 --> 00:02:10.225
- [Mark] How did this come about?

00:02:10.225 --> 00:02:13.260
- Well, it came about that
day two of my sobriety,

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:17.100
I went on Indeed, I activated my resume,

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.830
and I said, you know what?

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:21.359
I don't want to be one
check Norman anymore.

00:02:21.359 --> 00:02:24.570
You know, I want to be able
to be a productive citizen.

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:25.403
I wanna do something,

00:02:25.403 --> 00:02:27.429
and maybe my talk can inspire some people.

00:02:27.429 --> 00:02:29.600
Maybe I might get into a position

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:32.020
to where even if I get this job,

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:34.240
maybe a tenant has a problem

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.140
with a relative that is suffering.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.790
And maybe I can add, you know,

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:40.700
some type of inspiration or some hope.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:43.510
Or maybe they just need
somebody to talk to.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:46.270
And, you know, hopefully
prayerfully, I can be that.

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:49.525
- [Mark] Well, of the
2000 interviews I've done

00:02:49.525 --> 00:02:51.093
in the last 10 years,

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:53.580
when I was listening to yours,

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:56.140
it was just like this guy nails it better

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:57.108
than anyone I've spoken to.

00:02:57.108 --> 00:02:57.943
(Norman chuckles)

00:02:57.943 --> 00:02:59.070
And every, from every angle

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:00.607
when you mentioned
wherewithal, that was it.

00:03:00.607 --> 00:03:01.440
It was like that was it.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:02.273
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:02.273 --> 00:03:04.530
I kinda put that as that's my word.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:05.637
No, no one has ever really mentioned that

00:03:05.637 --> 00:03:07.220
in any of my talks.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.871
And that to me is the
most important thing.

00:03:09.871 --> 00:03:11.420
Not that, you know I'm not a drug user,

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:12.437
so I don't even know,

00:03:12.437 --> 00:03:14.940
but I know what it takes
to make anything happen.

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:17.740
It's not talent and it's not intelligence.

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:20.470
It's courage, certainly,
but really the core

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:22.300
of a lot of that in therapy

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.510
and getting the crap out of
your closet and all that stuff.

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:27.930
But the wherewithal, which
is the ability to do it.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:28.763
- Right.

00:03:28.763 --> 00:03:31.050
- [Mark] To get off the bed and
go do it every day is to me,

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:32.020
one of the most important things

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:32.930
that people don't understand.

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:36.460
- Yeah. An obstacle that
I have is, you know,

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:38.860
as far as housing is concerned, I mean,

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:40.940
I can stay with my buddy you know,

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:43.830
maybe three nights a week, you know?

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:45.730
So there's going to be
a point where I'm gonna-

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:46.750
- [Mark] But you've done this before.

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:47.583
- Yeah.

00:03:47.583 --> 00:03:48.920
- [Mark] You know how to
be a responsible citizen.

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:50.360
- Yeah. Where I have to,

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:52.080
we're probably going to
have to catch a train,

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:55.450
sleep on the train a
little bit, catch the bus.

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:56.407
- [Mark] Look at it as a challenge.

00:03:56.407 --> 00:03:57.900
- There's going to be an obstacle.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:58.850
And nobody says it's easy.

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:00.620
It's like a grand chess match.

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:03.840
You know, it's like, I've made a move.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:05.600
Now here comes another move.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:08.640
You know, it's not so much of
trying to get the checkmate,

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:09.723
but it's guarding.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.350
It's that guard that I got to put up.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:15.183
So I did call LAHSA.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:18.430
I left a message.

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:21.380
Maybe they can help me as far
as some housing is concerned.

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.320
We're just gonna do it, man.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:26.780
I mean, it's, you're
talking about 30 plus years

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:28.493
on and off, up and down.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:31.000
My kids need me.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.460
I did have a chance to
talk to my oldest daughter.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:35.870
She was very happy to hear from me.

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:38.543
She told me she loved me and
that made me feel real good.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.280
I had a chance to talk to my son,

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.780
who is the only son that I have.

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:47.320
He says, I don't give a damn what you do.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:48.710
You're always gonna be my father.

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:49.560
And that was good.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:52.637
And for you, sir, you...

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:57.240
You're almost, you might
be thought a photographer,

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:59.440
but I'm gonna call you a therapist.

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:01.090
And because what you did for me

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:04.493
is you allowed me to to
really get some shit out.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:07.310
You know, because I didn't want

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:08.970
to tell anybody about molestation.

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:10.960
I didn't want to tell
anybody about, you know,

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:13.160
I let a guy give me
some head for some money

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:16.080
because I'm looking at what
you gonna think about me

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:17.300
and what you're going to say about me.

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:18.510
And, you know, image is everything.

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:20.790
Now I'm a homeless crack
head, but image is everything.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:21.870
Well, guess what?

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:23.510
I don't give a fuck what you say about me.

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:25.720
What you say, think, and feel about me.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:26.673
There's two things.

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:30.240
The most important, this
is none of my business.

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:35.680
The second is, you're gonna
say what you wanna say.

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:36.700
You're gonna be judgemental.

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:38.470
And if you're gonna be
judgemental in life,

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:40.260
you're probably headed down a bridge

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:43.090
that's gonna soon blow up.

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:45.710
So man, I just, thanks.

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:46.770
- [Mark] No, I think,

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:48.010
you know you're not the first person

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:49.480
that's told me they stopped
using after talking.

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:51.010
And it's not that I'm
doing something magical.

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:53.970
I think it's, maybe I'm
not very judgmental.

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:55.900
And that, that opens the
door for you to tell me

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:57.790
all kinds of dirt that's in your closet.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.290
But it's that unloading
of all your baggage

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:03.080
that frees you up to go,

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:05.690
oh, I don't have to hide that any longer.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:06.523
- Right.

00:06:06.523 --> 00:06:08.950
- [Mark] And putting it
on a platform like YouTube

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:10.490
where basically in theory,

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:13.900
the entire world knows
now what you've done.

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:14.733
- Yeah.

00:06:14.733 --> 00:06:15.820
- [Mark] And that frees you up

00:06:16.844 --> 00:06:19.060
to not carry that heavy baggage around.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:20.260
- There were a couple of comments-

00:06:20.260 --> 00:06:21.180
- [Mark] To make decisions
like you just did.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.120
- Yeah. There were a couple of comments

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:24.740
where people were saying,
well, that's not the truth.

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:25.870
Then there was one person-

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:28.380
- [Mark] Every single one of
my videos on my channel is not,

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:30.400
I consider them, they're
not fully uploaded

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:32.260
until there's a comment saying it's a lie.

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:33.093
- Right.

00:06:33.093 --> 00:06:34.250
- And then one guy said that,

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:36.080
he said, look him up.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:37.170
It's true.

00:06:37.170 --> 00:06:38.860
Look at his Facebook page.

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:41.790
And then the other guy
says, get this boy back.

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:43.150
He's a billionaire.

00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:44.920
He's connected to Exxon.

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:48.830
You know, which a family
member founded Humble Oil,

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:50.470
which is now Exxon.

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:53.767
So I come from good stock
and you know, but sometimes,

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:57.690
hm how am I going to put this?

00:06:57.690 --> 00:07:00.070
If you turn the pot off,

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:02.760
you're not gonna have a fully cooked meal.

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:04.423
My pot has been turned off.

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:10.850
God has empowered me to
reach over to the stove.

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:14.400
But when I reach over to the stove,

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:15.710
it's not me guiding my hand.

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:17.340
It's him.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:18.950
See, I don't always
have to have it on high

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:20.473
to have a quick meal.

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:23.970
I can turn it on medium and cook it fully.

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:26.130
So I believe I'm being fully cooked.

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:27.350
I don't know where this stuff comes from.

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:28.400
It just comes out of my head.

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:29.233
You know?

00:07:29.233 --> 00:07:31.394
So I just want to do the best that I can.

00:07:31.394 --> 00:07:36.394
And we're gonna follow up again probably

00:07:37.339 --> 00:07:38.220
because they're probably going to say,

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:39.500
well hey, we want to hear from Norman.

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:40.480
And that was really, really great.

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:42.500
I think, you know, all of my life

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:45.700
and being in the upper
echelon of companies

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:46.533
and things like that,

00:07:46.533 --> 00:07:50.010
you never get a chance to really see

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:51.080
how people feel about you.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:53.690
Now these are people
who don't even know me.

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:55.600
And really, really, that was positive.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:57.800
And it turned me, it turned me.

00:07:57.800 --> 00:07:59.630
My buddy was like,
Norman, are you all right?

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:00.540
And I was just sitting there

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:02.480
and got tears just running down.

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:04.020
He's like, man, what's wrong?

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:05.860
I said, it's over.

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:06.693
He says, what?

00:08:06.693 --> 00:08:08.843
I said, it's over.

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:10.970
He said, I knew it.

00:08:11.980 --> 00:08:13.310
He said, I knew it.

00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:15.990
I knew it was going to
happen sooner or later.

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:18.560
And it doesn't matter if he doesn't stop.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:20.440
Maybe it's not his time.

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:25.080
And there's a scripture that
keeps ringing in my head.

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:26.780
Ecclesiastes 3:1.

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:29.923
There's a time, a purpose,
and a season for everything.

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.810
So I think this is my time.

00:08:33.810 --> 00:08:37.083
I don't fully understand
or really know my purpose,

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:40.700
but it's his season and I'm
gonna do the best I can.

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:43.870
- [Mark] You've got
everything it takes, I think.

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:45.337
- [Norman] Yeah, well
sometimes it can have

00:08:45.337 --> 00:08:48.023
everything that it takes
and it'll take away.

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:52.360
You know, I'm a very prideful person,

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:54.283
which now my pride is being stripped.

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:57.580
Because it's something that has been

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:59.290
not so much of an anomaly for me,

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:03.143
but it's been something that
has held me back, you know.

00:09:04.743 --> 00:09:07.040
Of course, you know,

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:10.940
being able to travel
and do all these things

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:12.670
and come from this family and all that,

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:15.420
I've been able to, you know,

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:17.410
enjoy the finer things in life.

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:19.030
And there were times where I had

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:20.730
a very pompous, arrogant attitude.

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:23.810
In the Rooms of Recovery,

00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:25.910
they say ego is edging God out.

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:28.797
I says, okay, well you know what?

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:32.360
I believe that God and I have
really settled our problem

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:35.160
because I had the problem with him.

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:37.480
He never had a problem with me.

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:40.430
And so I asked him, I
said, look if you're real,

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:43.253
if you are who you say you are, stop me.

00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:46.180
Stop me.

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:48.140
And you just work.

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:50.243
You work in me and I'll work for you.

00:09:52.125 --> 00:09:53.410
I don't want anymore.

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:54.610
I don't have a taste for it.

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:56.090
I could have money right now.

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:56.923
I don't want it.

00:09:56.923 --> 00:09:57.910
I've been offered it.

00:09:57.910 --> 00:09:59.390
One guy, he just couldn't believe it.

00:09:59.390 --> 00:10:00.570
He followed me all the
way down the street.

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:01.960
Norman, what's wrong with you?

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:03.420
You don't want any dope?

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:04.460
Dude, what's wrong?

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:06.960
I said, man, I don't want anymore.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:09.120
I said and I'll see you later.

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:11.870
And I remember walking down
